// An exponential mean pushed past itself by a fraction of the error its own
// second smoothing still carries, applied three times over.
//
// Exercises: a user function that holds per-bar state, called three times so
// that each call site keeps a state of its own, and the deepest warmup in this
// half of the gate: one layer is two averages and the layers nest three deep,
// so the first value is six averages of averages away from bar 0.

version 1

study("Sixfold smoothed", overlay = true, precision = 4)

len    = input(5,   "Length", min = 1, max = 1000)
factor = input(0.7, "Factor", min = 0, max = 1)

// Each call to this holds its own pair of averages, because a call site is
// where a stateful function's state lives. Writing the three layers out by hand
// would be the same arithmetic and three times the text.
fn layer(src, span, lift) =>
    first  = ema(src, span)
    second = ema(first, span)
    return first * (1 + lift) - second * lift

once   = layer(close, len, factor)
twice  = layer(once, len, factor)
thrice = layer(twice, len, factor)

plot(thrice, "Sixfold", purple, width = 2)
